  "goodToKnow": "Der Urwald is a primeval forest or jungle: der tropische Urwald, der Amazonas-Urwald. Germany has almost no true Urwald left, but since 2011 several ancient beech forests, including Hainich, Jasmund, Kellerwald, Serrahn and Grumsin, belong to a UNESCO World Heritage site. Hainich's slogan is Urwald mitten in Deutschland. The prefix ur- means original: die Urzeit, der Urgroßvater. Plural: die Urwälder."
